{"AuthzClientCryptoProvider#getBouncyCastleProvider creates a new KeyStore instance on each call just to obtain its provider; should cache this provider in a field or be explicit that this is not actually BouncyCastle to avoid repeated KeyStore instantiation.": 0.33519843220710754, "In AuthzClientCryptoProvider.ECDSACryptoProvider#concatenatedRSToASN1DER, the first two ASN1Encoder.create().write(...) calls are effectively no-ops and can be removed by reusing the same encoders passed into writeDerSeq.": 0.5707748532295227, "ECDSA test only checks that asn1derToConcatenatedRS and concatenatedRSToASN1DER are inverses of each other but never validates the result against JCA. Should extend the test to verify that a Signature instance accepts the re-encoded ASN.1 via verify to prove interoperability with JCA ECDSA implementation.": 0.516230583190918}